  "description": "Speed Without Sacrifice\nInspired by the medieval Scottish two-handed great sword, known for its strength and symbolism of the rugged Highlands, Deviate’s award-winning Claymore embodies this legacy - crafted to conquer the world's most challenging terrains.\nNow available in a new range of colours inspired by Scotland’s heritage, this long-travel enduro bike is as striking as it is capable.\nPerformance Where It Matters\nSharing the same carbon chassis as the Factory model, the Claymore Elite combines FOX 38 Performance Elite suspension, Shimano Deore 12-speed drivetrain, and DT Swiss E-1900 wheels with Continental Kryptotal tires for a reliable, high-performance ride at a more approachable price.\nAvailable in Morar Blue, In sizes M, L, XL, 29er or MX.\nLong Travel Enduro Race Bike, Now UDH\nThe Deviate Claymore continues its award-winning design while now being fully UDH compatible. This full-suspension mountain bike is built around a full-carbon frame designed for 29\" wheels front and rear with 165mm of rear travel. It's optimised for enduro racing, offering an unrivalled balance of high-speed control and excellent pedalling efficiency for all-day riding comfort thanks to our meticulously tested high-pivot suspension design. The frame works with both 170mm and 180mm forks.\nVoted Pinkbike's \"Enduro Race Bike of Choice 2022\"Winner of Singletrack's \"Editor's Choice Awards 2022\"\nUDH Compatible\nMedium Frame Only: Some fork damper adjusters may foul on the bottom of the downtube due to stack height, which varies brand to brand. To solve this you can purchase a crown race spacer here.",
